# Build outputs
bin/
obj/
_Module/bin/
TestResults/
out/

# Regenerated report artifacts: tools/validate_moduledata.py --json report.json
# (documented in .claude/rules/moduledata-validation.md) — never commit.
/report.json

# Visual Studio Edit-and-Continue / debug temp. VS dumps decompiled engine sources
# here while stepping (e.g. enc_temp_folder/<hash>/MissionState.cs). Never commit —
# a background auto-commit swept one in on 2026-06-14.
enc_temp_folder/

# Tool backups: rebalance/audit scripts write <file>.bak before destructive edits
# (see tools/README.md "XML I/O convention"). Git is the real backup — never commit these.
# The glob is *.bak* rather than *.bak because the newer scripts write dated
# sidecars (.bak-blacknum-20260817, .bak-parity-20260713, .bak-startergear) that
# a bare *.bak does not match. Two of those write inside the repo, so without the
# trailing * a `git add -A` would commit whole duplicate copies of the ModuleData
# XML (taom_partyTemplates.xml alone is 377 KB).
*.bak*
# Same class, different suffixes. `*.bak*` misses all of these: `.orig` is what a
# merge leaves behind, `~` is what most editors write, and `.backup` / `.old` are
# what a hand-copy gets named at 2am. None of the four has ever been tracked in
# this repo (checked 2026-09-01), so nothing is shadowed. Deliberately not adding
# *.tmp or *.save: those are scratch rather than backups, and the block is easier
# to reason about if it means one thing.
*.backup
*.orig
*.old
*~

# DR3 (2026-05-22): exceptions for bundled BUTR runtime DLLs in
# TAOM.Dependencies module. These are MAINTAINED-VENDOR — manually copied
# from Steam Workshop downloads (see docs/migration/dr3-maintenance.md) so
# the build is self-contained without external module dependencies. The
# locally-built TAOM.Dependencies.dll + .pdb still get ignored (regenerated
# on every build).
# Note: gitignore exceptions need the PARENT dirs un-ignored first because
# the top-level `bin/` rule matches everywhere.
!Dependencies/_Module/bin/
!Dependencies/_Module/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client/
# Gaming.Desktop sibling contains only build outputs (TAOM.Dependencies.dll +
# NuGet runtime deps) — fully ignored; Bannerlord on Windows reads Win64.
Dependencies/_Module/bin/Gaming.Desktop.x64_Shipping_Client/
# But still ignore everything in Win64 by default — only allow the
# specific BUTR-vendored DLLs.
Dependencies/_Module/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client/*
!Dependencies/_Module/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client/Bannerlord.ButterLib*.dll
!Dependencies/_Module/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client/Bannerlord.MBOptionScreen*.dll
!Dependencies/_Module/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client/Bannerlord.ModuleLoader.*.dll
!Dependencies/_Module/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client/BUTR.CrashReport*.dll
!Dependencies/_Module/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client/MCM.UI.Adapter.*.dll
!Dependencies/_Module/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client/Microsoft.Extensions.*.dll
!Dependencies/_Module/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client/Microsoft.Bcl.HashCode.dll
!Dependencies/_Module/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client/Serilog*.dll
!Dependencies/_Module/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client/System.Buffers.dll
!Dependencies/_Module/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client/System.Collections.Immutable.dll
!Dependencies/_Module/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client/System.Memory.dll
!Dependencies/_Module/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client/System.Numerics.Vectors.dll
!Dependencies/_Module/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client/System.Reflection.Metadata.dll

# Vendored runtime DLLs for Main module. Top-level `bin/` + `_Module/bin/`
# rules above ignore everything by default — un-ignore the specific DLLs
# we ship. TAOM.dll + TAOM.pdb stay ignored (build outputs, regenerated
# by `dotnet build`). MCMv5.dll is provided by TAOM.Dependencies + the
# Bannerlord.MCM NuGet — NOT vendored here. TAOM.NativeSkinFixes.dll is
# TAOM-owned C++ rebuilt outside this repo; drop the new .dll here and
# commit when it changes.
!Main/_Module/bin/
!Main/_Module/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client/
Main/_Module/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client/*
# BehaviorTrees.dll + BehaviorTreeWrapper.dll allowlists removed 2026-05-24 —
# both libraries are now inlined in TAOM source (Main/BehaviorTrees/ +
# Main/BehaviorTreeWrapper/) and compile into TAOM.dll. No standalone DLLs.
!Main/_Module/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client/MinHook.x64.dll
!Main/_Module/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client/TAOM.NativeSkinFixes.dll
# Gaming.Desktop sibling: build outputs only — stays ignored.
Main/_Module/bin/Gaming.Desktop.x64_Shipping_Client/

